{"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Declaring-a-macro","title":"Declaring a macro","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro","doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetRecordMacro"]},{"anchor":"Diagnostics","title":"Diagnostics","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The expansion behind every linker-set macro, for clients that declare a kind and a macro of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their own."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LinkerSetEntry(kind:)"},{"type":"text","text":" takes its kind as an argument. A client that registers one kind of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thing (routes, events, migrations) gives it a macro that fixes the kind instead, so its users"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route"},{"type":"text","text":" and never see a number. That takes three declarations."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The client’s compiler plugin, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".macro"},{"type":"text","text":" target that depends on this module, names the kind:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import LinkerSetsMacroSupport","import SwiftCompilerPlugin","","@main","struct RoutesMacrosPlugin: CompilerPlugin {","    let providingMacros: [any Macro.Type] = [RouteMacro.self]","}","","public enum RouteMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x726F_7574 }  \/\/ \"rout\"","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The client’s library declares the macro, the same kind, and the read of the set. It depends on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSets and re-exports it, because the expansion calls LinkerSets’ ","type":"text"},{"code":"#linkerSetRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"users’ files:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@_exported import LinkerSets","","extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let routes = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)  \/\/ \"rout\"","}","","@attached(peer)","public macro Route() = #externalMacro(module: \"RoutesMacros\", type: \"RouteMacro\")","","extension Endpoints {","    public static var all: [Endpoint] {","        LinkerSet<Endpoint>(kind: .routes).values","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Its users then register routes and read them through the library:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["enum Endpoints {","    @Route static let home = Endpoint(path: \"\/\")","}","","let endpoints = Endpoints.all"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"What the re-export exposes","level":3,"anchor":"What-the-re-export-exposes","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route static let home = ..."},{"text":" expands, in the user’s file, to one call:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#linkerSetRecord(kind: 0x726F7574, storing: Self.home)"},{"text":". That macro, which LinkerSets declares,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"expands in turn to the record itself, one declaration per object format, naming","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetsRuntime.LinkerSetRecord"},{"text":". So the user’s file has to see LinkerSets. With","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@_exported import LinkerSets"},{"text":" in the client’s library, importing the client is enough. With a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plain or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"public import"},{"text":", every user’s file fails to compile with “no macro named","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"‘linkerSetRecord’” until it imports LinkerSets itself. The compile tests in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tests\/CompileFailures"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ExportingClientUser"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ImportingClientUser"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ImportingClientUserImportingLinkerSets"},{"text":") check each case.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So every file that imports the client also sees "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetKind"},{"type":"text","text":" and anything"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"public the client adds to them. A kind constant doesn’t need to be public: the macro writes the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"kind as a number, so users’ files never name the constant. Keep it internal and give users the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values through the client’s own API, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Endpoints.all"},{"type":"text","text":" does above. A user can still read the set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by its number, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)"},{"type":"text","text":"; an internal constant only keeps it out of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"autocomplete and out of the client’s public API."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro"},{"text":" writes the same record ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LinkerSetEntry"},{"text":" writes, in the same section, and its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"diagnostics name the client’s attribute (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"'@Route' applies to static members only"},{"text":"). Each kind","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a set of its own, so two clients in one program never see each other’s records as long as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their kinds differ. Kind 0 is reserved, and the expansion refuses it.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Registering types","level":3,"anchor":"Registering-types","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A macro attached to a struct, enum, class or actor stores the type’s metatype. To read the types","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as a protocol they share, without casting, the plugin names that protocol in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/requiredConformance(of:)"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Events.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record then holds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"any AnalyticsEvent.Type"},{"type":"text","text":", read with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values"},{"type":"text","text":". A type that doesn’t conform fails to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compile where it’s declared: “cannot convert value of type ‘NotAnEvent.Type’ to type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"‘any AnalyticsEvent.Type’”. Qualify the protocol with its module so a type of the same name at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the use site can’t stand in for it. Without a required protocol, a type’s record holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Any.Type"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A registered type can be nested in another from swift-syntax 600 on. Before 600 a macro can’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"see where its declaration sits, so the type must be declared at file scope.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A macro that takes its kind as an argument can return "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kindArgument(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kind(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"Declaring the kind once","level":3,"anchor":"Declaring-the-kind-once","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin returns the kind from "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/kind(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and the library reads the set by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, so the number appears twice, and a mismatch shows only at run time, as an empty set. To write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it once, put it in a module of its own that depends on nothing, and have both import it:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ RoutesKind","public enum RouteKind {","    public static let rawValue: UInt32 = 0x726F_7574  \/\/ \"rout\"","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ RoutesMacros, the plugin","public enum RouteMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { RouteKind.rawValue }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Routes, the library","extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let routes = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: RouteKind.rawValue)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The package lists the module among both targets’ dependencies:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".macro(name: \"RoutesMacros\", dependencies: [\"RoutesKind\", ...])","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".target(name: \"Routes\", dependencies: [\"RoutesKind\", \"RoutesMacros\", ...])","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". SwiftPM builds it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for the host for the plugin and for the target for the library.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Testing the expansion","level":3,"anchor":"Testing-the-expansion","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A client’s expansion tests pin one line per record, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#linkerSetRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" call:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["assertMacroExpansion(","    \"\"\"","    enum Endpoints {","        @Route","        static let home = Endpoint(path: \"\/\")","    }","    \"\"\",","    expandedSource: \"\"\"","    enum Endpoints {","        static let home = Endpoint(path: \"\/\")","","        #linkerSetRecord(kind: 0x726F7574, storing: Self.home)","    }","    \"\"\",","    macroSpecs: [\"Route\": MacroSpec(type: RouteMacro.self)],","    failureHandler: { Issue.record(\"\\($0.message)\") }",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"assertMacroExpansion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" expands only the macros in its table, so the call stays as written, and it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads the same on every swift-syntax from 600 on. The record behind it, one declaration per object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"format, belongs to LinkerSets and changes when LinkerSets adds a format. A test that wants it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anyway adds ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"linkerSetRecord\": MacroSpec(type: LinkerSetRecordMacro.self)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to the table. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declaration at file scope expands to the call inside a private enum of its own, whose name comes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the context’s unique names (","type":"text"},{"code":"__macro_local_15linkerSetRecordfMu_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Writing the expansion yourself","level":3,"anchor":"Writing-the-expansion-yourself","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" supplies the peer "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expansion"},{"type":"text","text":". A macro that needs more writes its own and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"calls "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/recordPeers(of:providingPeersOf:in:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" from it for the record. That’s how"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a macro adds the conformance as well, so its users write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event struct Login {}"},{"type":"text","text":" without naming"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the protocol. The macro takes an extension role beside the peer:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro, ExtensionMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Events.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","","    \/\/ The record, as a peer.","    public static func expansion(","        of node: AttributeSyntax,","        providingPeersOf declaration: some DeclSyntaxProtocol,","        in context: some MacroExpansionContext","    ) throws -> [DeclSyntax] {","        try recordPeers(of: node, providingPeersOf: declaration, in: context)","    }","","    \/\/ The conformance the record requires, as an extension.","    public static func expansion(","        of node: AttributeSyntax,","        attachedTo declaration: some DeclGroupSyntax,","        providingExtensionsOf type: some TypeSyntaxProtocol,","        conformingTo protocols: [TypeSyntax],","        in context: some MacroExpansionContext","    ) throws -> [ExtensionDeclSyntax] {","        [try ExtensionDeclSyntax(\"extension \\(type.trimmed): Events.AnalyticsEvent {}\")]","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The library declares the macro with both roles:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@attached(peer)","@attached(extension, conformances: AnalyticsEvent)","public macro Event() = #externalMacro(module: \"EventsMacros\", type: \"EventMacro\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A type can then carry data of its own through the protocol (a schema, a name) while the record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holds only its metatype, read as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"Skipping a record instead of refusing it","level":3,"anchor":"Skipping-a-record-instead-of-refusing-it","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The expansion refuses what a record can’t hold with an error. A macro that would rather skip some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of those (a generic event that its library lists by hand, say) asks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/refusal(of:providingPeersOf:in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" first. It returns a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic"},{"type":"text","text":" whose "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic\/reason-swift.property"},{"type":"text","text":" says why, and whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic\/node"},{"type":"text","text":" is where to report it, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when the declaration can hold a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public static func expansion(","    of node: AttributeSyntax,","    providingPeersOf declaration: some DeclSyntaxProtocol,","    in context: some MacroExpansionContext",") throws -> [DeclSyntax] {","    if let refusal = try refusal(of: node, providingPeersOf: declaration, in: context),","       refusal.reason == .genericType {","        context.diagnose(Diagnostic(node: refusal.node, message: GenericEventNote()))","        return []","    }","    return try recordPeers(of: node, providingPeersOf: declaration, in: context)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every other refusal still reaches ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/recordPeers(of:providingPeersOf:in:)"},{"text":", which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"throws it. Where a declaration sits (in a function’s body, a protocol or a generic type) is seen","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from swift-syntax 600 on; before it those three aren’t returned, and the compiler refuses them in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the expansion.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport"}],"title":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"LinkerSetsMacroSupport","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://LinkerSetsMacroSupport/documentation/LinkerSetsMacroSupport/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic","title":"LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport\/linkersetmacrodiagnostic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why a linker-set macro refuses a declaration or a kind, with the message the compiler shows,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"naming the macro as it was written ("},{"code":"@Route","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), and the node the message points at."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LinkerSetMacroDiagnostic","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://LinkerSetsMacroSupport/documentation/LinkerSetsMacroSupport/LinkerSetRecordMacro":{"title":"LinkerSetRecordMacro","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport\/linkersetrecordmacro","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetRecordMacro","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSetRecordMacro"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSetRecordMacro"}],"abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#linkerSetRecord(kind:storing:)"},{"text":": one record of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kind"},{"text":" whose accessor stores the expression,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written in the section LinkerSets owns, under ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#if objectFormat(...)"},{"text":" with one declaration per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"object format.","type":"text"}]},"doc://LinkerSetsMacroSupport/documentation/LinkerSetsMacroSupport/LinkerSetMacro/recordPeers(of:providingPeersOf:in:)":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"recordPeers(of:providingPeersOf:in:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsmacrosupport\/linkersetmacro\/recordpeers(of:providingpeersof:in:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/documentation\/LinkerSetsMacroSupport\/LinkerSetMacro\/recordPeers(of:providingPeersOf:in:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The record that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"declaration"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes, as a peer, for a macro that writes its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expansion"},{"type":"text","text":" and calls this from it: to add a condition first, or beside another role, such"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as an extension that adds a conformance."}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"recordPeers","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"of","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11SwiftSyntax09AttributeB0V","text":"AttributeSyntax","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"providingPeersOf","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11SwiftSyntax04DeclB8ProtocolP","text":"DeclSyntaxProtocol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"in","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiftSyntaxMacros21MacroExpansionContextP","text":"MacroExpansionContext","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11SwiftSyntax04DeclB0V","text":"DeclSyntax","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}]},"doc://LinkerSetsMacroSupport/documentation/LinkerSetsMacroSupport/LinkerSetMacro/refusal(of:providingPeersOf:in:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"refusal"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11SwiftSyntax09AttributeB0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AttributeSyntax"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"providingPeersOf"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11SwiftSyntax04DeclB8ProtocolP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DeclSyntaxProtocol"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiftSyntaxMacros21MacroExpansionContextP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MacroExpansionContext"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":